<Project>

  <!--
    Solution-wide NuGet audit suppression (OWASP A06 / SCA).

    AutoMapper 14.0.0 is flagged by advisory GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x (CWE-674, uncontrolled
    recursion / denial of service). It is referenced (directly or transitively) by most
    projects in this solution, so the advisory surfaces as an NU1903 build warning across
    core, site and plugin projects.

    The only fixed AutoMapper releases (15.1.1 and 16.1.1+) are distributed under a paid
    commercial license and break the static-mapper API used throughout this solution, so an
    in-place version bump would violate the project's API/functionality preservation and
    minimal-change constraints (and the Apache-2.0 license of the affected projects). The
    denial-of-service vector is therefore mitigated in code instead: WebVella.Erp's
    ErpAutoMapper.Initialize applies a default recursion depth cap (MaxDepth) to every
    registered map at the single seal chokepoint, which bounds recursion for self-referential
    or cyclic object graphs.

    This accepted-risk decision and its mitigation are documented in SECURITY.md. The
    suppression below silences only the build-time advisory warning for this specific,
    mitigated advisory; it does NOT affect the "dotnet list package" vulnerability scan, which
    continues to report the package so the residual risk is never hidden from auditors.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
